Insight

    Some aircraft types show higher severe damage rates
        Accidents cluster in certain regions
        Seasonal and weekly patterns exist
        A small number of operators account for more severe incidents

    By what percentage 
        Reduce financial losses
        Minimize fatal incidents
        Choose safer aircraft types

Recommendation

    Prioritize aircraft types with historically low accident rates
    Invest in newer aircraft models with modern safety systems
    Consider manufacturer safety history as a procurement criterion
    Avoid aircraft categories frequently linked to severe or fatal incidents

        Prefer aircraft types with lower severe damage & fatality rates
         Avoid high-risk operating regions where possible
         Investigate safety history of aircraft operators
         Consider seasonal risk in operational planning

Next Steps
        Consider seasonal risk in operational planning
